+## Workflow
+
+1. Derive the HTTP contract before editing: methods, paths, status codes, wire
+   shapes, and size limits. This step is done when every requested endpoint or
+   client call has an observable public-boundary outcome.
+2. Implement the smallest code that satisfies that contract, using the
+   applicable server or client rules below.
+3. Verify the contract at the HTTP seam with `httptest`. This step is done when
+   every applicable outcome has been observed: endpoints restricted to GET
+   return 405 for HEAD; array responses encode as `[]` for nil, empty, and
+   no-match input; and bodies larger than a strict response limit are rejected.
+   Report any outcome that the available tools cannot verify.
+
